## 3. Composite scoring

**Composite metric:** {{COMPOSITE_METRIC}}
<!-- COMPOSITE_METRIC: how the per-node primary metrics roll up into the
     headline number. One of:
       - `terminal`  — the terminal node's metric is the headline (the
         pipeline's output is what the terminal node produces).
       - `mean`      — unweighted mean of the per-node primary metrics.
       - `weighted`  — weighted mean (per-node weights in COMPOSITE_WEIGHTS).
       - `min`       — the worst node gates (bottleneck).
     `terminal` is the recommended default (a pipeline's output is the
     terminal node's output); the others suit pipelines where every node's
     own quality matters to the headline. Per-node scores are ALWAYS reported
     in addition to the composite. Filled during /spp-init from the user's
     stated success criterion. -->

**Composite weights:** {{COMPOSITE_WEIGHTS}}
<!-- COMPOSITE_WEIGHTS: required only when COMPOSITE_METRIC is `weighted` —
     one weight per node id (e.g. `craft: 1.0, respond: 2.0`); a node's
     missing weight defaults to 1.0. Use `n/a` for any other composite
     metric. -->

**Composite floor:** {{COMPOSITE_FLOOR}}
<!-- COMPOSITE_FLOOR: optional floor on the composite metric, or `none`. Each
     node also carries its own floor in its plan.md; the pipeline ships only
     when every node's floor is met (and the composite floor, if set). -->

