## 4. Sequencing and freezing

Nodes are optimized **in order, upstream-frozen**. A node is optimized with the
ordinary single-prompt loop and **frozen** when its loop reaches the node's
**dev stop criterion / floor** — a **loop-level** freeze, on dev, **not** a
per-node `/spp-finalize`. The frozen node's prompt is then run over the data to
materialize the next node's baseline. Downstream optimization never changes an
upstream node. There is **exactly one `/spp-finalize`** — the composite finalize
at the end of the pipeline — and it is **the only sacred-test read** (#6/#7): no
node reads the test partition during its loop, and there is no per-node finalize
(DESIGN.md §7.1.12).

