## Validation rules

A `pipeline.md` is **correctly filled** when all of the following hold. The
Phase 4 template linter verifies these mechanically; the designer agent
verifies them at the pipeline's G1.

1. All `{{...}}` placeholders are resolved (no remaining `{{` or `}}` outside
   this validation list).
2. `PIPELINE_NAME` is kebab-case, contains no spaces or slashes.
3. The nodes form a **linear chain**: at least two nodes, in a total order;
   each node after the first declares exactly one upstream node; no cycles; no
   fan-in or fan-out. General DAGs are out of scope (DESIGN.md §7.1.12).
4. Each node's task directory exists at `sub-tasks/<NODE_ID>/` and contains a
   valid `plan.md` (the per-node contract; validated by that plan's own rules).
5. Every upstream-output input mapping references a real output field
   (an OUTPUT_SCHEMA field) of a node that appears **earlier** in the order.
6. Node 1 has no upstream mapping — it reads only original baseline columns.
7. `COMPOSITE_METRIC` is one of `terminal`, `mean`, `weighted`, `min`;
   `weighted` requires per-node `COMPOSITE_WEIGHTS`.
8. Every node has **node-local gold** (its `plan.md` defines an OUTPUT_SCHEMA
   and a metric). End-to-end-only labeling (a terminal-only gold requiring
   credit assignment across nodes) is out of scope (DESIGN.md §7.1.12).
9. The pipeline revision log has at least one row, with monotonically
   increasing `PIPELINE_VERSION` integers.
